 "description": "Use this when someone asks what is showing in one area tonight, tomorrow, this weekend or on a date. Reads ONE regional board per call; SceneF publishes 56 boards, in California, Florida and Hawaii only. Pass region; it defaults to \"sf\" (San Francisco) when omitted. For a city, ZIP or neighborhood, call scenef_resolve_board first. Returns a ranked list of films, with optional genre and format filters. When the window covers tonight it opens with Notable tonight: scarcity facts with evidence (measured seat counts, final nights, lone prints, posted discounts, live elements). Each entry carries year, runtime, genres, a one-line hook, venue count, showtime_count, the next showtime and the film's SceneF url. \"detailed\" adds showtime rows, about 200 across the answer; scenef_search_showtimes lists the times for one film or theater. Read-only: the call itself records nothing. SceneF does not sell, hold or book tickets. Ticket links are https://scenef.com/go/{id} redirects to the theater's own site or the ticket seller it uses (a link to a showtime that is gone lands back on SceneF); whoever follows one, a person or a client, is logged once anonymously (time, the screening with its film and theater, client type, browser family, referring site, link source tag, and whether the showtime was gone; no IP address, cookie or account) and forwarded. Every emitted showtime carries confidence, source tier, reporting sources and verified_at.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "properties": {
   "formats": {
    "description": "Format/tag filters, e.g. [\"35mm\", \"70mm\", \"qa\", \"live-score\"].",
    "items": {
     "maxLength": 80,
     "type": "string"
    },
    "maxItems": 10,
    "type": "array"
   },
   "genres": {
    "description": "Genre filters, e.g. [\"horror\", \"comedy\"].",
    "items": {
     "maxLength": 80,
     "type": "string"
    },
    "maxItems": 10,
    "type": "array"
   },
   "max_results": {
    "description": "Max films to return (default 12, cap 25).",
    "maximum": 25,
    "minimum": 1,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "region": {
    "description": "Which regional board to read: a board id such as \"sf\", \"oahu\" or \"miami\", not a city name (\"Honolulu\" or \"Chicago\" is rejected). Omitted means \"sf\" (San Francisco); it is never inferred from where you are. For a city, ZIP or neighborhood call scenef_resolve_board first; scenef_now with no region lists every id. An unknown region is an error, not a fallback.",
    "maxLength": 120,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "response_format": {
    "description": "Output size. \"concise\" (default) is tight text plus a structured summary. In whats_playing, each film has the total showtime_count, next_showtime, and a showtimes array containing only that next screening; \"detailed\" adds showtime rows with ids, ticket urls and accuracy metadata, about 200 across the answer. film_details and search_showtimes return the 40 nearest showtimes in \"concise\" and up to 200 in \"detailed\". showtime_count is always the total and showtimes_complete says whether the array is all of it; narrow by date or theater for the rest.",
    "enum": [
     "concise",
     "detailed"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "when": {
    "description": "When to look: \"tonight\" (default), \"tomorrow\", \"weekend\" (Fri/Sat/Sun of the current week), or a YYYY-MM-DD date.",
    "maxLength": 120,
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "type": "object"
 },
